The suspected Dream Market main administrator was arrested in Germany on German money-laundering charges in a coordinated German and US effort, with IRS-CI and DEA Miami investigating and the BKA Cybercrime Unit and ZKI Oldenburg assisting; the FBI, USPIS and HSI belonged to the 2016-2022 task force. Only the US indictment ties him to the administrator role, the 2022 transfers went into new consolidated wallets, and the searches located about $1.2 million in identified accounts and wallets rather than seizing that sum in cryptocurrency.
